  "id": "u05-l08",
  "unit": "u05-numbers-time",
  "title": "Days of the week",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Every day ends in **-বার** (*-bar*, 'day of the week'), and like English the names come from the sun, moon and planets:\n\n**রবিবার** Sun-day · **সোমবার** Moon-day · **মঙ্গলবার** (Mars) · **বুধবার** (Mercury) · **বৃহস্পতিবার** (Jupiter) · **শুক্রবার** (Venus) · **শনিবার** (Saturn)\n\n**আজ কী বার?** = 'What day is it today?' **দিন** is 'day' in general: **সাত দিন** 'seven days'. **সপ্তাহে** means 'in a week': **এক সপ্তাহে সাত দিন**.\n\n**কাল** (*kal*) means **both 'yesterday' and 'tomorrow'**; a verb's tense tells you which. With no verb, as in **কাল শনিবার**, it means 'tomorrow'.\n\n*Culture:* the weekly holiday in Bangladesh is **শুক্রবার** (Friday), the day of Jumma prayers. Many offices close on **শনিবার** too, so the working week runs Sunday to Thursday.",
